    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d324">

                <pb facs="0471" n="379" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v01/pg379"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72119/2251</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Minister in Switzerland</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Stovall</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-10-22T12:00:00-04:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 22, 1918, noon</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>5173. Your 5277, October 18, 6 p.m.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d324-f1"/> Department
                    cannot authorize discussions with anyone representing Emperor
                        Charles, either in official or unofficial capacity.
                    Refer to this Government’s reply of October 18 [<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >19</hi>]<anchor n="2" xml:id="d324-f2"/> to Austrian peace proposal.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
